scripts/vendor with LTM_VENDOR_HOST_ONLY=1 builds only the host binaries: the native dependencies, usbmuxd, QEMU's
dylib, iBoot32Patcher and ipod-helper into Frameworks/ and MacOS/ (with include/ and dSYMs/), checked against
macOS 11 by codemod.py's native rules, and leaves Resources/Guest, Device, licenses and usbmuxd-conf empty. The
Big Sur build takes its resources from the official release (install.sh), so it needs neither the SecureROMs, the
armv6 and iPad SDKs, the guest tools, the developer tools nor the built-in iPod's IPSW, and its checks don't ask for
them. It leaves ANGLE out (patch 22): QEMU is built without the ANGLE renderer and Frameworks/ has no libEGL or
libGLESv2. It still writes the machine options (MachineOptions.swift) from the dylib it built, which Xcode's first
phase compares. vendor.json records host-only, so a full run afterwards builds the rest.

